    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>aura compiler programming-language cli</tags>
    <summary>Compiler and tools for the Aura programming language</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Aura is a statically typed, compiled programming language with Python-like syntax.

This package installs the `aura` command for x86-64 Windows, together with the native runtime that `aura build` links into programs:

- `aura run` and `aura build` compile a program to a native executable.
- `aura check`, `aura fmt`, `aura test` and `aura verify` check, format, test and prove programs.
- `aura lsp` serves the Aura extension for Visual Studio Code.

## Notes

- `aura build` and native `aura run` link programs with the Microsoft linker. Install the Visual Studio Build Tools with the "Desktop development with C++" workload, for example with `choco install visualstudio2022buildtools visualstudio2022-workload-vctools`. `aura check`, `aura fmt`, `aura run --backend mir` and the language server need no linker.
- Aura is a technical preview, so its versions are prereleases. Install and upgrade with `--pre`.
- Upgrade with `choco upgrade aura --pre`, not `aura upgrade`.
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
